# Exact cached post-live --all findings; answers explain only the anchors of their class.

[ceiling] These two 6.30 mm diameter blind underside storage sockets have CAD roofs at Z 2.25 and mate the 6.00 mm basin pegs with 0.15 mm radial / 0.25 mm nominal top air. They are distinct from the exterior expanding R6 surface. In the existing R6 native slice, each first roof at nozzle Z 2.60 has 17 Bridge deposits and no support; the 0.24 mm model step gives nominal underside Z 2.36. R6 keeps its supports-off exterior transition recipe. Physical bridge shape and docking force remain unmeasured.
alternatives: Through or open-sided sockets remove this bridge but cut another source face or reduce gravity-parked engagement. Arched socket roofs need a different mating peg/air convention. A separate bed-facing socket block adds an assembly joint while preserving the outer source round.
