[thin] These exact surfaces bound the 2.30 mm left wall of the open interior top storage key, from X -8.45 to X -6.15 at Z 18.207. This is the reference's top docking adaptation, not the expanding show round or a spring wall. The top key is open through its upper face; the current R6 recipe holds Classic walls, 0.24 body/0.08 top band, six walls in the expanding band, wall-first and 15% overlap. The accepted tee result concerns bottom appearance only, not this docking wall's load or life.
alternatives: A narrower or shifted interior key gives a larger side wall while retaining the exterior source curve, but needs a matching H key and seating-clearance review. A wider source column adds stock externally and changes the represented source section. A separate top saddle preserves the source body with another interface and part.
